WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.719
A café sells forty smoothies at three dollars each. How much money comes in?

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:19.347
Total revenue is all the money a firm receives from selling its output. Multiply price by quantity sold. Three times forty is one hundred and twenty dollars.

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:28.503
You can rearrange it. Quantity is revenue divided by price. One hundred and twenty dollars divided by three dollars is forty smoothies.

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:39.311
If sales are given week by week, add them first. Forty, fifty-five and forty-five make one hundred and forty. Then one hundred and forty times three is four hundred and twenty dollars.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:51.660
Steps one and two. Find the selling price and the quantity sold. Ignore any cost per unit or average cost: costs are not revenue.

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:59.801
Steps three and four. Multiply price by quantity, write the working, and give the answer with the currency sign.

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:18.533
Here is a real question from June 2023. A firm sells its product at seventy-five euros a unit, with a cost per unit of thirty-five euros. Calculate total revenue when monthly sales are two hundred and fifty units. Two marks.

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:25.018
Pick out the price and the quantity. The cost of thirty-five euros is a distractor: costs are not revenue.

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:35.901
Seventy-five times two hundred and fifty is eighteen thousand seven hundred and fifty euros. Write the euro sign. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:43.248
A common mistake is multiplying by the cost per unit instead of the price.

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:47.042
Another is leaving out the currency sign on the final answer.

00:01:48.160 --> 00:02:08.171
Now you try. A bakery sells cupcakes at two dollars fifty each. It sells one hundred and twenty on Saturday and eighty on Sunday. Each cupcake costs ninety cents to make. Calculate total revenue for the weekend. Pause here and work it out.

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:18.659
Add the sales first: one hundred and twenty plus eighty is two hundred cupcakes. Ignore the ninety-cent cost.

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:22.148
Two dollars fifty times two hundred is five hundred dollars.

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:27.599
Check it. Saturday brings three hundred dollars and Sunday two hundred: five hundred in total.

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:36.905
Remember: find price and quantity, ignore the costs, multiply, and add the currency sign. Now try the practice questions.
